<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
license:BSD-3-Clause
copyright-holders:MAMEdev Team

RC702 display layout — TRUE RC752 (NEC JB-1201M(A)) geometry.

The RC752 monitor's active display area is 230 x 165 mm (RCSL 44-RT1981) for the
8275's 560 x 275 visible raster (80 cols x 7 dots, 25 rows x 11 lines).  That is
a physical aspect of 230:165 = 46:33 = 1.3939, i.e. pixel aspect ratio 0.685
(pixels ~1.46x taller than wide).

The background-colour margin around the active raster is baked into the screen
bitmap by screen_update_with_border (rc702.cpp) via bitmap.fill(palette[0]) and
a CRTC_BORDER coordinate offset in display_pixels.  No separate artwork element
is needed; the margin is renderer-independent (SDL and BGFX both correct).

View 776x568 with screen filling the full bounds.  The 8-pixel bitmap margin
(CRTC_BORDER) scales proportionally with the content.
-->
<mamelayout version="2">

	<view name="Standard">
		<bounds x="0" y="0" width="776" height="568" />
		<screen index="0">
			<bounds x="0" y="0" width="776" height="568" />
		</screen>
	</view>

</mamelayout>
